# {{PRODUCT_NAME}} evaluation data

Keep domain evaluation data separate from the base corpus. Before modifying retrieval, routing,
prompts, or provider behavior, create and review:

- development cases for rapid iteration;
- validation cases for threshold and design decisions;
- held-out test cases that are not used for debugging;
- answerable, refusal, permission, prompt-injection, conflicting-source, and domain-risk slices.

Record data provenance, review owner, sensitivity classification, and the exact base commit used.
Never commit customer documents, API keys, provider responses containing sensitive text, or exported
production conversations.
